# Moss turf 3: a messy, sprawling heap of sun-dried moss about 0.5 m tall and 0.8 m across, nine lumps of straw-yellow and olive
# moss piled round a dark hummock of teal, with seven sporophyte stalks leaning out of it. Late summer to the other moss turfs'
# spring, the counterpart of grass-turf3.
# Few, chunky shapes rather than a bristle of fine ones, so it stays light enough to scatter by the hundreds.
format 1

# Detail as the grass and flowers have it: the fine stalks and thin stems are small next to the model's size
Detail detail=0.4
    Intersection
        Union
            Material material=moss_soil
